    "updated_at": "2025-10-24T15:22:28Z",
    "body": "> Can I have a link to the spec PR for this change for more details?\n\nIt was done by https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/8253. More specifically, the checks were moved from step 10 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/14f9d9867610292b6361a557ade3487f782d612d/#creating-a-javascript-module-script to step 7 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/90c74b72ce27a8ac6cfad82c45f5bbee9e522ae4/#hostloadimportedmodule.\n\nThe reason for this is that ECMA-262 needed to be able to be the one deciding when to load a module's dependencies, so I moved the dependencies check in HTML from when the module is created to when we actually load its dependencies.\n\n> Do we also re-try successful resolutions?\n\nNo, because once a resolution is successful ECMA-262 will not ask HTML anymore to resolve it (step 2.d.ii of https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-InnerModuleLoading).\n\nTo be more precise, we do not retry a resolution if the whole loading of that individual module was successful. If the module resolves correctly but then fails loading, we would re-try resolving it (and it would then find the corresponding cached loading error).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
